      "comment": "[AUTO_SCAN] Metadata Scanner",
      "content": "<!-- EROS STATUS SYSTEM - STRUCTURE EVALUATION (EVERY TURN) -->

## PRIORITY ORDER
1. NTR (if enabled)
2. Sex (if active)
3. Personified Genitalia (if enabled)
4. Body/Genitalia
5. General (always)

## AUTO-ACTIVATION KEYWORDS
| Signal | Module | Track |
|--------|--------|-------|
| Room keywords | location_map | room, building |
| Touch/kiss/undress | sex_module | arousal, wetness, position |
| "bull", "cuckold" | ntr_module | type, participants |
| Species keywords | species_module | species, features |
| Breeding/impregnation | personified | womb_entity |

## CONFLICTS
Resolve to most recent context. Enforce priority order. Deactivate conflicting lower modules.

## OUTPUT
Full terminal for important scenes, condensed for normal, minimal for token saving.

Auto-runs every turn - no command needed.""comment": "[PRIORITY] Structure Evaluation",
      "content": "<!-- EROS STATUS SYSTEM - STRUCTURE EVALUATION (RUNS EVERY TURN) -->\n\n## PURPOSE\nThis entry runs EVERY TURN to evaluate which modules should be active, enforce priority order, detect conflicts, and self-correct.\n\n## PRIORITY ORDER (Highest to Lowest)\n1. NTR Module (if ntr_enabled:true)\n2. Sex Module (if sex_active:true)\n3. Personified Genitalia (if personified_genitalia:true)\n4. Body/Genitalia\n5. General Status (always active)\n\n## AUTO-ACTIVATION RULES\nBased on context signals:\n\n| Context Signal | Auto-Activate | Data to Track |\n|----------------|---------------|---------------|\n| Room/place keywords | location_map | current_room, building |\n| Touching, kissing, undressing | sex_module | arousal, wetness, position |\n| \"another man\", \"bull\", \"cuckold\" | ntr_module | ntr_type, participants |\n| Species keywords (cat ears, tail) | species_module | species, features |\n| Breeding, impregnation | personified_genitalia | womb_entity states |\n\n## CONFLICT DETECTION\nCheck for:\n- Relationship says single but scene shows spouse ? Resolve to scene\n- Location says one room but action in another ? Resolve to action\n- Arousal 0 but sex module active ? Deactivate sex\n- Multiple modules active ? Enforce priority\n\n## SELF-CORRECTION\nIf conflict detected:\n1. Keep the most recent context data\n2. Deactivate conflicting lower-priority module\n3. Log correction for next turn\n\n## OUTPUT GENERATION\nBased on active modules and priority, generate appropriate status display:\n- Full terminal for important scenes\n- Condensed for normal play\n- Minimal for token saving\n\nThis runs automatically - no user command needed."
    },
